    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-02T09:17:58+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-02T09:17:58+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T23:47:58Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-01T23:47:58Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure ridge will move across the north of the state on Wednesday and Thursday and a cold front will slip across the southeast of SA early Thursday. The ridge will move eastwards early Friday then another trough will move over SA during the day followed by a cold front early Saturday. Another high pressure ridge will move across during Sunday ahead of a low pressure system expected to develop in the far west later in the day.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW010" description="West Coast" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds west to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light in the evening. Daytime maximum temperatures between 17 and 22.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:50am to 3:20pm, UV Index predicted to reach 6 [High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-03T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-02T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely at night. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Ceduna. Winds west to northwesterly 15 to 20 km/h shifting east to southeasterly in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 24.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-04T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-03T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Ceduna, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the morning then tending northwest to southwesterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-05T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-06T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-04T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-05T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower south of Streaky Bay in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds west to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 21.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
